VCF Generation Pipeline for NGS Data Analysis
Project Overview

This project automates Variant Call Format (VCF) generation from Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) data using a reproducible bioinformatics workflow. The pipeline processes raw sequencing data, performs alignment and variant calling, and generates standardized VCF output for downstream genomic analysis.

The goal of this project is to create an efficient and scalable workflow that reduces manual intervention and enables faster genomic variant identification.

Objectives
Automate processing of raw sequencing files.
Generate high-quality VCF files from sequencing reads.
Standardize genomic analysis workflow.
Enable reproducibility using containerized execution.
Support future integration with APIs and web applications.
Features

✅ FASTQ input handling
✅ Sequence alignment to reference genome
✅ BAM generation and sorting
✅ Duplicate marking
✅ Variant calling workflow
✅ VCF generation
✅ Automated output storage
✅ Docker-compatible execution
✅ Scalable pipeline architecture

Workflow Architecture
Input FASTQ Files
        ↓
Quality Check (optional)
        ↓
Sequence Alignment (BWA)
        ↓
SAM → BAM Conversion
        ↓
Sorting & Indexing
        ↓
Duplicate Removal
        ↓
Variant Calling
        ↓
VCF Generation
        ↓
Output Storage
